  "id": "gr-kamoshirenai",
  "connector": "〜かもしれない",
  "gloss": "might; probably",
  "title": "〜かもしれない・〜でしょう — maybe, probably",
  "pattern": "plain form (noun / な-adjective without だ) + かもしれない / でしょう (casual: だろう)",
  "explanation": "かもしれない means “might”: {雨|あめ}が{降|ふ}るかもしれない — it might rain. でしょう is “probably”, a little more sure: {明日|あした}は{晴|は}れるでしょう — it’ll probably be fine. Nouns and な-adjectives go straight before them: {雨|あめ}かもしれない, {静|しず}かでしょう. In casual speech, かも alone and だろう are common.",
  "natural": "Hedging softens everything: ちょっと{遅|おく}れるかも — I might be a bit late.",
  "stiff": "Weather-report でしょう sounds formal in chat. With friends, たぶん…と{思|おも}う is more natural.",
